# Phase 620 — `VerifyDocSnippets` extracts every in-scope ```fsharp block
# from the docs into `docs-snippets/generated/`. Those files are build
# output reproducing a doc's text verbatim, so formatting them is both
# meaningless and actively wrong: `dotnet fantomas --check .` would fail
# on any repo where the target had been run, over source nobody wrote.
docs-snippets/generated/
**/docs-snippets/generated/

# Phase 787 — `proofs/oracle/RemotingDecode.fs` is the F* extractor's output,
# reproduced byte for byte by `proofs/check.ps1` and compared against the
# committed copy. Formatting it would break that diff on every run, over source
# nobody wrote. Same class as the generated doc snippets above. Phase 790's
# `DisclosureFold.fs` is the second extraction, held by the same byte-diff.
proofs/oracle/RemotingDecode.fs
proofs/oracle/DisclosureFold.fs
# The proof leg's working directories: the downloaded toolchain, F*'s
# .checked cache, and the fresh extraction the byte-diff compares. All
# gitignored, but Fantomas reads THIS file rather than .gitignore, so a
# developer who has run the leg would otherwise fail dotnet fantomas
# --check . on output nobody wrote.
proofs/.fstar/
proofs/.cache/
proofs/.extract/
